Apple marketing chief Greg Joswiak today shared an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> video that offers a look at how "Resident Evil" director Zach Cregger uses an iPhone during filmmaking.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/resident-evil-apple-tv.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075753" /><br/>
Cregger said he uses his iPhone and <a href="https://www.cadrage.app">the Cadrage app</a> to plan out filming sequences ahead of time. He decides what shots to take, what lenses to use for each shot, and what's in each frame. He then prints out the images so the crew knows exactly what to do.<br/>
<br/>
According to Cregger, he used this process for "Weapons" and "Barbarian," two movies that he wrote and directed. He said every scene in those films was planned with photos in advance.<br/>
